# Lambda invoke output
# out.json is the conventional name for `aws lambda invoke` output, and the
# price checker's deploy script suggests exactly that command as a test run. Its
# response body carries real user data — wishlist titles, product URLs, and
# hashed user_ids for every user with a triggered alert — so a locally generated
# copy must never be committed. The /*.json rule is anchored to the repo root so
# any similarly-named response dump is caught too; nested JSON is unaffected.
out.json
/*.json

# Jupyter
.ipynb_checkpoints/
